From: Cyryl Sochacki <cyrylsochacki@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] udev: release the simulated pointer after the last touch contact

When a touch contact ends, staging_active has already been decremented,
so "staging_active == 0" is true exactly when the last finger was lifted.
The pointer was therefore reported as pressed after release and released
while a second contact was still down. The menu acts on pointer release,
so taps on a touchscreen did nothing (tested on Allwinner A20 with an
FT5x06 touchscreen, KMS + udev, RetroArch 1.20.0).

Keep the pointer pressed while any contact is active, as the comment says.

---
--- a/input/drivers/udev_input.c
+++ b/input/drivers/udev_input.c
@@ -2402,7 +2402,7 @@
             /* Simulated pointer */
             /* Release the pointer only after all contacts are released */
             if (touch->pointer_enabled)
-               touch->pointer_btn_pp = (touch->staging_active == 0);
+               touch->pointer_btn_pp = (touch->staging_active > 0);
 
             /* Mouse section */
             if (touch->mouse_enabled)
